# Lab 5 – Smart Color Detection & Control with MIT App Inventor


**Course:** Internet of Things (IoT)

**Project:** Lab 5 – Smart Color Detection & Control with MIT App Inventor

---

# Project Overview

This project implements a smart color detection and control system using an ESP32 programmed in MicroPython. The system reads colors using the TCS34725 RGB sensor, classifies the detected color, controls a NeoPixel RGB LED ring, adjusts a DC motor speed using PWM, and communicates with a MIT App Inventor mobile application for monitoring and manual control.

---

# Hardware Used

- ESP32
- TCS34725 RGB Color Sensor
- NeoPixel Ring (16 LEDs)
- DC Motor
- L298N Motor Driver
- Jumper Wires
- USB Cable
- WiFi Network

---

# Software Used

- Thonny IDE
- MicroPython
- MIT App Inventor
- VS Code

---

# System Workflow

1. ESP32 initializes all peripherals.
2. TCS34725 continuously reads RGB values.
3. ESP32 classifies the detected color.
4. NeoPixel changes to the detected color.
5. Motor speed changes according to the detected color.
6. The detected color is displayed in the MIT App.
7. The user can manually control the motor and NeoPixel from the app.

